Z||000000||tinuvin||07-18-2001||12:14 PM||||while driving my 84 indy home last night, i got a ticking noise coming from the engine. then the car died. after having it towed home, i took the oil filler cap off of the valve cover, turned it over, and saw no movement of internal parts. what am i looking at replacing here? any guesses? <BR>thanks||||reg||9
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||07-18-2001||12:18 PM||||Sounds like timing componets.<BR>Crank and cam gears.||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||07-18-2001||12:55 PM||||yes definetly timing gear.I dont think it is any thing like a rod.||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||07-18-2001||07:55 PM||||Timing gears stripping are pretty common. This subject was discussed in length earlier and I believe the last word was that valve train damage would likely result(don't know if it applies to all engs) from timing component failure while at highway speeds.(bent valve stems, etc) Search the archives for timing gear failures. I wouldn't go turning the eng over till you have further investigated the timing. Good luck, keep forum informed of outcome, we like to hear GOOD news.<BR>Don<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000004||Rodrv6||07-18-2001||08:18 PM||||Speaking from experience, the stock 4 cylinder will not suffer any damage to the valve train when the timing gear breaks.  I've had this happen no less than 3 times over the years and two of those happened on the highway at 70 mph plus.  I finally put a set of all steel gears in it, so it shouldn't happen again.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||7
Z||000005||maryjane||07-18-2001||08:27 PM||||Thanks for clarifing that Rod, I couldn't remember what eng was being discussed in the other thread. I hate giving out bum scoop.<BR>Don||||reg||7
Z||000006||West Coast Fiero||07-18-2001||08:32 PM||||any mileage over 140,000 would make me lean towards a broken cam, however you didnt say what your mileage was or maybe I missed it||||reg||1
